  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mississippi recorded $6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state has 85,905 awards so far, with an average award size of $69.7K. Obligations are down 25.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $5B, and Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry by obligations at $3.7B. HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED is the largest vendor by obligations at $3.6B. These figures reflect fiscal year to date totals and are partial for the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buying agencies in Mississippi?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $5B in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $350M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $161M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $86M and the Department of Homeland Security at $79.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries capture the most federal dollars in Mississippi?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing captured $3.7B in FY2026 to date. Other top industries include Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $507M and Facilities Support Services at $169M. Construction-related industries together show significant obligations, for example Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $155M and Industrial Building Construction at $115M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Mississippi?",
      "a": "Mississippi received $6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 85,905 awards with an average award size of $69.7K. Obligations are down 25.2% year over year and these totals are partial for the current fiscal year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Mississippi?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, and the Department of Veterans Affairs award the most contracts in Mississippi. The Department of Defense obligated $5B, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $350M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $161M in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Mississippi?",
      "a": "HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED, V2X AEROSPACE LLC, and NOVA SPACE SOLUTIONS, LLC are the largest federal contractors in Mississippi by obligations. HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED received $3.6B, V2X AEROSPACE LLC received $466M, and NOVA SPACE SOLUTIONS, LLC received $109M in FY2026 to date."
